  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="c9718f5f-91fc-5d00-97b2-72a328346d33" activityNameId="012bc6ee-7c11-5ecf-b135-7392f74df8bf" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Molybdenum, at regional storage</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Molybdenum, at regional storage
Molybdenum is used e.g. in catalytic converters. It is not used for alloying steel. For this, molybdenum trioxide or molybdenite is used. For a lack of specific data, the metallurgical process of the zinc production is used as a proxy. Only the input of the concentrate is adapted. Although zinc and molybdenum concentrate are both sulfidic and the metal content is almost the same, this is a crude assumption and the data quality therefore is poor.;
Formula: Mo; 
UUID: 848c158a-8a4f-3206-a772-ac344d3454f9
The module includes the production of high grade primary molybdenum by pyro- and hydrometallurgical processes, the disposal of the slag and the treatment of the waste water.
Location: undefined
Technology: A mix of 80% hydrometallurgical and 20% pyrometallurgical production of zinc is chosen to represent the molybdenum production
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_848c158a-8a4f-3206-a772-ac344d3454f9.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
